Subject: [PATCH] P-105b: review asks by recognition the letter forms a lesson
 only traced

A letter lesson asks some forms only by tracing. Unit 2's l-2 never
asks se medial or final, jeem isolated or final, che initial, baRi-he
initial or final, or khe isolated by picking or naming them, and seven
review sittings still left four of those never recognised: review picks
a form by index and never looks at what the lesson asked. 33 letters
across the nine letter lessons have such a form (learning review,
2026-10-23). Asking more inside the lesson would lengthen it about as
much as it helps (2026-10-22); review is where the gap is.

`recogniseGaps` finds, once, from the letter lessons themselves, the
forms each letter's lesson never asks by recognition (by glyph, so a
non-joiner's identical forms count once). In review, and when a letter
is woven into another lesson, a letter with such forms is asked one of
them on two turns in three, by naming then picking; the third turn is
as before, tracing included. Letters without gaps are asked as before;
lessons and their lengths are unchanged.

The first version took tracing out of review for those letters; a
review with only letters due then went to 52% "which position", past
check:shape's 40%, so one turn in three stays as it was. The case
against: the rule does not know when a gap is filled, so review keeps
steering to those forms; naming a position is labelling, not reading.

Tests: the gaps are forms l-2 never recognises; ten sittings ask every
one; l-2 keeps its tracing. The coverage test fails with review on the
old chooser (checked). check:shape passes.

